WEBVTT

00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:05.150
In the early morning of the 29th,

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:08.690
after 17 days of fighting,

00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:10.990
Phoinike surrendered to Balt-Rhein.

00:00:12.070 --> 00:00:14.030
It was a complete and utter defeat.

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:15.700
Thank you.

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:17.240
Is there anything else?

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:19.950
That is all we received from Capitan Brega.

00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:21.870
I see.

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:23.710
Furthermore, Capitan Brega has taken

00:00:23.870 --> 00:00:26.790
Tughril Mahmut Bey
of the Torqye Pashalu

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:30.260
and Phoinike's Kaisaras' eldest son,
Kiros Ios Apollodorus into custody

00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:32.510
in honor of our alliance with Phoinike.

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:34.430
Did you say Torqye?

00:00:34.970 --> 00:00:37.100
His name sounds familiar.

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:41.430
He was involved in the uprising in Hisar,
and had his position as Pasha stripped away.

00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:43.640
I remember now.

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:46.480
It's the Pasha who despises war.

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:48.860
I see.

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:10.460
Altair: A Record of Battles

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:23.200
I welcome you, Mahmut Pasha.

00:02:23.370 --> 00:02:24.540
No, pardon me.

00:02:24.830 --> 00:02:31.460
I believe you are currently serving the Seventh
Province's Halil Pasha as his Binbashu.

00:02:31.670 --> 00:02:33.670
Yes, that is right, Doge Lucio.

00:02:34.130 --> 00:02:36.630
You are well-informed.

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:39.010
I am glad you were able to escape to safety.

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:40.300
Doge Lucio.

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:42.800
Allow me to be blunt.

00:02:43.390 --> 00:02:49.100
Why did you betray the alliance
between Phoinike and Venedik?

00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:51.900
During times of peace,

00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:57.070
Phoinike would economically support
Venedik's trade and commerce,

00:02:57.240 --> 00:02:59.240
and guaranteed the safety of our merchants.

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:03.410
In exchange, we would organize
and immediately deploy a fleet in times of war

00:03:03.830 --> 00:03:06.870
if we were ever called upon for reinforcements.

00:03:07.540 --> 00:03:09.620
But you never came.

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:12.500
The exact wording of our treaty is as follows:

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:15.460
"When there is a call for reinforcements,

00:03:15.630 --> 00:03:19.130
the allied nation
is to deploy a fleet immediately."

00:03:19.550 --> 00:03:22.640
Nowhere does it say
that the fleet must arrive.

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:27.180
What the hell are you talking about?
What kind of scam are you running?

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:31.060
Then what of this situation?

00:03:31.730 --> 00:03:34.900
Let us suppose that within a day
of sending a distress signal,

00:03:35.020 --> 00:03:37.020
Phoinike fell?

00:03:37.190 --> 00:03:39.400
It's not like Phoinike fell in a day!

00:03:39.740 --> 00:03:41.780
We fought for 17 days!

00:03:41.950 --> 00:03:44.160
You can't tell me you didn't have the time!

00:03:44.320 --> 00:03:49.160
Doge, the Empire now has complete control
of the western Centro's waters.

00:03:49.790 --> 00:03:53.000
Is this not a serious blow to Venedik?

00:03:53.210 --> 00:03:56.630
I would like to know your thoughts
on this matter.

00:03:56.790 --> 00:03:58.590
Let's see.

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:01.420
Our famous Venedik glass

00:04:01.590 --> 00:04:04.470
cannot be made without the crystals
from Phoinike.

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:11.770
However, Phoinike will surely continue to mine
for high quality crystal year after year.

00:04:12.690 --> 00:04:17.520
We certainly would be greatly troubled if they were
to suddenly stop selling us these crystals.

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:19.150
Do you understand?

00:04:19.690 --> 00:04:25.030
Venedik is perfectly capable of forming
a trade agreement with the Balt-Rhein Empire.

00:04:26.120 --> 00:04:27.240
The Empire is a nation

00:04:27.410 --> 00:04:30.790
that invaded and destroyed your allies
without just cause.

00:04:31.330 --> 00:04:33.080
Would you trust such a nation

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:36.080
and do business with them,
only to be deceived in the end?

00:04:37.290 --> 00:04:38.540
Mahmut Bey.

00:04:39.250 --> 00:04:44.720
It is not as if we entered an alliance
with Phoinike out of trust.

00:04:46.050 --> 00:04:47.930
And that is how you feel,

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:51.890
even after Phoinike's Magistros was killed
by the hands of the Imperial soldiers.

00:04:53.180 --> 00:04:54.770
Did you not know?

00:05:01.940 --> 00:05:05.610
Do you not feel anything
after your friend's life

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:08.240
was so callously taken by the Empire?

00:05:08.700 --> 00:05:10.120
Mahmut Bey.

00:05:10.240 --> 00:05:13.830
In other words, you mean to say
we should fight the Empire?

00:05:14.210 --> 00:05:18.710
Are you saying you have no issue
with all Centro nations falling to the Empire?

00:05:19.090 --> 00:05:20.340
No.

00:05:20.550 --> 00:05:25.260
I am asking why you only assume
the Empire must be fought.

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:27.760
If the Imperial Army marches towards us,

00:05:27.930 --> 00:05:30.180
we will naturally face them without mercy.

00:05:30.350 --> 00:05:33.470
However, as long as
they do not meet us with hostility,

00:05:33.640 --> 00:05:36.270
we will not make war with them either.

00:05:36.440 --> 00:05:41.860
Besides, the Empire is not a simple group
of mass murderers.

00:05:42.280 --> 00:05:45.530
We could raise the flag of surrender
from the very start.

00:05:45.700 --> 00:05:48.700
That is also an option.

00:05:48.870 --> 00:05:51.620
Just as Phoinike so wisely decided.

00:05:51.740 --> 00:05:52.740
You little--

00:05:52.910 --> 00:05:55.910
You do not understand
the ruthlessness of these invaders.

00:05:56.120 --> 00:05:59.920
I am aware that the Empire
destroyed your homelands.

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:02.380
Then I would ask you,

00:06:02.550 --> 00:06:06.760
is it justified to make war
in the name of stopping war?

00:06:06.920 --> 00:06:09.430
Whether you invade another nation,
or protect your own,

00:06:09.590 --> 00:06:11.800
is war still not war?

00:06:12.140 --> 00:06:15.810
Our city, which maintains peace and prosperity
without fighting,

00:06:15.980 --> 00:06:19.690
is this not your ideal nation,
in a matter of speaking?

00:06:21.230 --> 00:06:22.770
What do you think?

00:06:22.980 --> 00:06:27.150
Why don't you spend some time in our city
and see for yourself?

00:06:30.820 --> 00:06:33.200
I knew it going in, but I'm still angry!

00:06:33.370 --> 00:06:35.490
He's exactly the sly fox
people said he was.

00:06:35.660 --> 00:06:37.910
All talk and evasive.

00:06:38.080 --> 00:06:43.040
No, the Doge's views on international relations
are logically sound.

00:06:43.210 --> 00:06:45.250
Are you saying he's the right one in this?

00:06:45.500 --> 00:06:46.510
No.

00:06:46.670 --> 00:06:48.970
I am simply saying
there are many right answers.

00:06:49.130 --> 00:06:52.640
Well, you'll never convince me he's right.

00:06:52.850 --> 00:06:55.850
I want to learn more about Venedik.

00:06:56.020 --> 00:06:59.730
I have to see if the people of this nation
are truly only cold and calculating.

00:06:59.890 --> 00:07:02.810
I think that's pretty clear
after meeting the Doge.

00:07:03.230 --> 00:07:06.820
But I did sense that he was somewhat affected
by the news of the Magistros' death.

00:07:06.980 --> 00:07:08.530
I don't know about that.

00:07:09.030 --> 00:07:10.910
Let's search for a Water Shrine.

00:07:11.070 --> 00:07:13.570
We should meet with the kulak
stationed here and get--

00:07:13.740 --> 00:07:15.660
There are no kulaks in this city.

00:07:22.380 --> 00:07:24.670
Masquerade of Sincerity

00:07:25.170 --> 00:07:28.550
I see that the merchants lead the military here.

00:07:28.710 --> 00:07:30.260
That is right.

00:07:30.420 --> 00:07:33.890
Business in the Centro
is fraught with danger.

00:07:34.050 --> 00:07:35.260
Be it pirates,

00:07:35.430 --> 00:07:37.140
be it foreign armies...

00:07:37.470 --> 00:07:39.980
In other words,
those most familiar with naval combat

00:07:40.140 --> 00:07:43.440
are the merchants and their crew.

00:07:43.600 --> 00:07:46.110
If a fight should break out,

00:07:46.270 --> 00:07:49.900
the firms with the deepest connections
to where the battle takes place

00:07:50.070 --> 00:07:52.070
are the ones to organize
and deploy a fleet.

00:07:52.490 --> 00:07:54.030
Your homeland...

00:07:54.200 --> 00:07:58.200
The Phoinike region
is Brega Company's turf.

00:07:59.290 --> 00:08:02.080
If you're so familiar
with the wind and the tides,

00:08:02.580 --> 00:08:05.670
then couldn't you have made it to Phoinike
in five days?

00:08:05.840 --> 00:08:08.880
Why are there no kulaks in this city?

00:08:09.050 --> 00:08:13.470
While I was on a pirate hunt
near Phoinike five years ago,

00:08:13.590 --> 00:08:16.140
I met an interesting Torqyean man.

00:08:17.930 --> 00:08:20.220
-Suleyman Bey?
-That's right.

00:08:22.810 --> 00:08:24.940
It seems he took a liking to me,

00:08:25.100 --> 00:08:27.650
and he invited me to join
the Torqye's spy network.

00:08:27.820 --> 00:08:31.860
But in Venedik,
every port we do business in

00:08:32.070 --> 00:08:34.530
has a bulletin board
and a guild outpost.

00:08:34.700 --> 00:08:37.370
I saw one of those bulletin boards
at the port.

00:08:37.530 --> 00:08:39.490
Each company Capitan

00:08:39.660 --> 00:08:44.080
has a duty to share the information
he or she learned on their voyage.

00:08:44.620 --> 00:08:49.840
In other words, you already have something similar
to a spy network created through national policy.

00:08:50.800 --> 00:08:53.670
I bet that put Suleyman Bey
in an awkward position.

00:08:53.840 --> 00:08:56.930
I told him that Venedikians
are a collection of people

00:08:57.050 --> 00:09:00.140
who can only live in Venedik.

00:09:00.770 --> 00:09:03.060
There is not a single person in Venedik

00:09:03.770 --> 00:09:06.810
who would ever betray the nation
that's given them a home

00:09:06.980 --> 00:09:08.900
for some other foreign country.

00:09:09.110 --> 00:09:10.400
That's what I told him.

00:09:10.610 --> 00:09:15.490
How could we do business with foreign nations
in order to bring the most benefit to our own?

00:09:15.610 --> 00:09:19.030
That is all we Venedikians and the Doge
have on our minds.

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:22.080
It doesn't matter who the other party is,
it is all the same.

00:09:22.200 --> 00:09:23.620
In other words,

00:09:23.790 --> 00:09:26.420
Venedik does not show favoritism
with other nations.

00:09:26.620 --> 00:09:27.790
That's right.

00:09:28.170 --> 00:09:31.170
Even if it is an allied nation.

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:36.430
Then there's nothing we can say to a Doge like that
to change his mind.

00:09:36.590 --> 00:09:38.930
Mahmut Bey,
we should just pack up and lea--

00:09:39.100 --> 00:09:41.180
Oh, that's too bad.

00:09:42.010 --> 00:09:45.520
It seems that Venedik wasn't to your liking.

00:09:46.190 --> 00:09:47.690
Hi, Cecilia.

00:09:47.850 --> 00:09:49.020
Welcome.

00:09:49.190 --> 00:09:51.940
You have some unusual guests
with you today.

00:09:53.400 --> 00:09:56.030
This is Capitan Brega's wife.

00:09:56.450 --> 00:09:58.320
The Capitan put me up in his home

00:09:58.490 --> 00:10:01.490
when I first arrived in the city.

00:10:01.660 --> 00:10:06.210
Abiriga is like a son to us.

00:10:08.080 --> 00:10:14.090
My real parents sold me to traders in Tharros
when I was 13.

00:10:16.220 --> 00:10:17.550
He's from Tharros.

00:10:17.720 --> 00:10:19.590
These injuries aren't serious,

00:10:19.800 --> 00:10:21.510
but he's severely malnourished.

00:10:25.680 --> 00:10:27.520
Capitan, are you okay?

00:10:30.940 --> 00:10:33.610
Capitan, incoming Tharros ship!

00:10:34.360 --> 00:10:37.400
Well, if it isn't an honored Capitan
from Venedik.

00:10:37.570 --> 00:10:40.610
Are you intending to abduct
our valuable slave?

00:10:42.620 --> 00:10:44.830
That should be more than enough.

00:10:44.990 --> 00:10:48.250
That's worth five times the price
of a normal slave.

00:10:48.790 --> 00:10:52.170
This boy's potential
is worth the investment.

00:10:52.920 --> 00:10:56.050
Abiriga is the one who scarred
my husband's face.

00:10:56.380 --> 00:10:58.170
And I cannot apologize enough.

00:10:58.880 --> 00:11:01.140
But thanks to him, I gained my freedom.

00:11:01.300 --> 00:11:06.430
I am hoping to pay back the money
the Capitan spent to buy me before he dies.

00:11:06.640 --> 00:11:09.020
But it's hard going with my pay...

00:11:11.150 --> 00:11:12.730
This alarm...

00:11:13.900 --> 00:11:15.480
A ship has been in an accident.

00:11:15.650 --> 00:11:16.940
It's the Colonna Company!

00:11:17.110 --> 00:11:19.530
They lost their entire cargo in a storm!

00:11:19.700 --> 00:11:20.700
Colonna Company?

00:11:23.530 --> 00:11:26.200
It has been a long time, Abiriga.

00:11:26.580 --> 00:11:33.460
I have come to discuss the return
of the 540 ducats you borrowed from me.

00:11:34.920 --> 00:11:40.880
This man borrowed money from me
in order to invest in a spice deal.

00:11:41.090 --> 00:11:44.680
You were supposed to make a profit
from the shipment to Colonna,

00:11:44.850 --> 00:11:46.510
but now you're left with nothing.

00:11:46.890 --> 00:11:51.020
And I understand that you don't even
have insurance?

00:11:51.810 --> 00:11:55.650
-Yes, you--
-That's right.

00:11:56.020 --> 00:12:00.280
A man who has no right to invest
wouldn't be allowed to have insurance.

00:12:00.820 --> 00:12:04.490
You have violated the Republic's trade laws.

00:12:04.660 --> 00:12:07.490
Anyone in a company's employ

00:12:07.660 --> 00:12:11.790
is not allowed to invest in a different firm.

00:12:12.120 --> 00:12:14.670
Abiriga, why did you do such a thing?

00:12:15.880 --> 00:12:18.840
I cannot say.

00:12:20.260 --> 00:12:21.720
I see.

00:12:22.550 --> 00:12:26.720
Those who break our trade laws
will be exiled without exception,

00:12:26.890 --> 00:12:29.350
no matter what reason they may have had.

00:12:30.020 --> 00:12:33.100
Your official trial will be held tomorrow.

00:12:33.270 --> 00:12:36.440
You should take the time
to pack your things now.

00:12:41.940 --> 00:12:42.950
Abiriga.

00:12:43.280 --> 00:12:46.820
Why did you not tell the Capitan
the real reason?

00:12:47.280 --> 00:12:50.580
The reason you were willing to break the law
and invest in another company

00:12:51.120 --> 00:12:54.330
was because you wanted to pay back
the money the Capitan spent on you.

00:12:54.920 --> 00:12:58.090
If I did that, the Capitan would save me.

00:12:59.130 --> 00:13:02.300
If he helped a criminal like me
for personal reasons,

00:13:02.420 --> 00:13:05.760
he would lose the trust of Venedik's citizens,

00:13:05.930 --> 00:13:07.680
and find himself without a place here.

00:13:08.300 --> 00:13:12.560
Losing the Capitan
would be detrimental to Venedik.

00:13:12.730 --> 00:13:15.730
In that case, it would be better
to accept the blame myself.

00:13:16.270 --> 00:13:20.730
Taking responsibility for my crime
and repaying the debt

00:13:20.900 --> 00:13:23.030
is the best course of action for the nation.

00:13:24.030 --> 00:13:24.990
Come in.

00:13:27.870 --> 00:13:31.200
We are taking you into custody
until your trial begins.

00:13:31.410 --> 00:13:33.370
Would you please come with us?

00:13:33.540 --> 00:13:35.910
Yes, I am ready.

00:13:36.080 --> 00:13:37.250
Goodbye then.

00:13:37.460 --> 00:13:40.000
Thank you for your help.

00:13:40.170 --> 00:13:42.000
If you follow this map,

00:13:42.170 --> 00:13:45.260
it will lead you to the lodging house
that's been arranged for you.

00:13:46.550 --> 00:13:49.010
Please stop looking so dejected.

00:13:49.180 --> 00:13:52.260
I've got no sympathy
for that lanky bastard.

00:13:52.430 --> 00:13:56.980
He knowingly committed a crime after being
lured by the promise of immediate gains.

00:13:57.390 --> 00:13:59.360
It is not that I am dejected.

00:13:59.520 --> 00:14:01.730
Then what are you thinking about?

00:14:02.110 --> 00:14:05.780
I am thinking about the two sides
of the people here.

00:14:08.950 --> 00:14:12.030
It's a shame what's happened.

00:14:12.370 --> 00:14:17.660
Nobody could have foreseen
such a cascade of misfortune.

00:14:18.960 --> 00:14:22.380
And he was so easily deceived.

00:14:22.710 --> 00:14:26.010
We told him the Capitan was sick
with only three months to live,

00:14:26.670 --> 00:14:29.220
and he believed such a lie!

00:14:29.340 --> 00:14:32.810
Honestly, Tharrosians are so simple-minded!

00:14:33.890 --> 00:14:35.560
Is that so?

00:14:36.270 --> 00:14:38.390
Well, well, if it isn't Mahmut Bey.

00:14:38.730 --> 00:14:40.850
What did you mean just now?

00:14:41.020 --> 00:14:43.270
It should be clear if you were listening.

00:14:43.480 --> 00:14:46.780
We set Abiriga up.

00:14:47.400 --> 00:14:50.700
Abiriga has caused our friends
quite a bit of pain over the years,

00:14:50.910 --> 00:14:53.450
and he's honestly been a nuisance.

00:14:53.620 --> 00:14:56.660
I hope you know that
I won't be keeping this quiet.

00:14:56.870 --> 00:14:58.290
Feel free to do whatever you like.

00:14:59.580 --> 00:15:02.250
Telling lies that leave no evidence.

00:15:02.420 --> 00:15:05.380
Not stopping an individual
from committing a violation.

00:15:05.710 --> 00:15:08.470
Neither of these actions breaks Venedik law.

00:15:09.010 --> 00:15:11.720
Although, I'm not sure
how things work in Torqye.

00:15:15.970 --> 00:15:19.940
Okay, it seems there is some room
for sympathy.

00:15:20.100 --> 00:15:22.810
Let's help Abiriga.

00:15:24.360 --> 00:15:28.070
I cannot stand by and do nothing
after what they've said.

00:15:28.940 --> 00:15:31.570
I thought you'd say that.

00:15:32.700 --> 00:15:34.370
What are you planning to do?

00:15:34.530 --> 00:15:37.040
If they're using their merchant tactics,

00:15:37.200 --> 00:15:40.080
then I will fall back on my military tactics.

00:15:43.380 --> 00:15:46.340
Everything has been going smoothly so far.

00:15:46.500 --> 00:15:48.090
I see.

00:15:48.260 --> 00:15:49.470
But, Capitan,

00:15:49.630 --> 00:15:51.470
you didn't need to do all of this.

00:15:51.800 --> 00:15:54.890
Everyone in this city
knows what you've accomplished.

00:15:55.050 --> 00:15:57.470
If they hear of your sudden departure
overseas,

00:15:57.680 --> 00:16:01.140
it will gather unwanted attention.

00:16:02.480 --> 00:16:05.270
"Abiriga was formally exiled."

00:16:05.440 --> 00:16:10.490
This is a necessary step in order for everyone
to perceive that as the truth.

00:16:10.690 --> 00:16:14.410
Now, all that's left is to see how
Mahmut Bey will proceed.

00:16:15.700 --> 00:16:17.780
-Not there!
-Wait!

00:16:18.990 --> 00:16:21.210
My God, just how much is he betting?

00:16:21.370 --> 00:16:23.210
The actual match is even more impressive!

00:16:23.420 --> 00:16:27.380
It's one versus 20,
and that kid's actually winning!

00:16:27.880 --> 00:16:29.170
Checkmate!

00:16:29.380 --> 00:16:30.460
This is checkmate as well.

00:16:30.670 --> 00:16:34.970
Checkmate! Checkmate! Checkmate!

00:16:35.180 --> 00:16:37.220
This should...

00:16:37.430 --> 00:16:38.640
Checkmate!

00:16:39.930 --> 00:16:42.770
It seems that you have quite the hobby.

00:16:42.940 --> 00:16:45.810
I've had some experience
through my military training.

00:16:45.980 --> 00:16:48.730
Although, this is my first time
playing for money.

00:16:49.230 --> 00:16:50.730
Now, as promised,

00:16:51.570 --> 00:16:54.240
this prize of 700 ducats is mine.

00:16:55.110 --> 00:16:58.240
Like hell it is!
You'd better watch it, outsider!

00:16:58.410 --> 00:17:00.240
Put that money back down on the table.

00:17:00.450 --> 00:17:01.500
You brats!

00:17:01.660 --> 00:17:03.620
You're not getting out of here alive!

00:17:04.000 --> 00:17:05.250
Okay, that's enough.

00:17:06.080 --> 00:17:09.380
I hope you all remember
whose establishment you're in.

00:17:09.550 --> 00:17:11.630
Now, why don't you two
put your money away?

00:17:12.170 --> 00:17:14.630
Be careful on your way back to your lodging.

00:17:15.840 --> 00:17:18.260
-Goodbye.
-Thank you very much.

00:17:19.470 --> 00:17:22.180
-I can't believe it.
-I lost so much money.

00:17:22.350 --> 00:17:23.680
What happened here?

00:17:23.850 --> 00:17:27.190
I don't know what you all are up to,

00:17:27.440 --> 00:17:30.150
but that boy's got some guts.

00:17:33.280 --> 00:17:36.030
The ship will be leaving in an hour.

00:17:36.240 --> 00:17:39.740
Mahmut Bey never did show up in the end.

00:17:39.910 --> 00:17:43.290
It seems that we had the wrong assumption.

00:17:56.090 --> 00:17:58.010
That's 700 ducats.

00:17:58.550 --> 00:18:03.140
I will pay for all of Abiriga's debts
to the Capitan and Mora.

00:18:03.520 --> 00:18:06.940
Therefore, I would like Abiriga
acquitted and released.

00:18:09.560 --> 00:18:12.900
Mahmut Bey, actually,

00:18:13.280 --> 00:18:16.070
there is something I must confess to you.

00:18:16.240 --> 00:18:17.780
I'll tell them.

00:18:18.530 --> 00:18:20.030
Tell us what?

00:18:20.240 --> 00:18:23.040
I apologize for our deception.

00:18:23.580 --> 00:18:29.370
We were testing you to see whether or not
we could entrust you with Abiriga.

00:18:29.540 --> 00:18:30.830
What did you say?

00:18:31.000 --> 00:18:33.300
Then all of that was an act?

00:18:33.670 --> 00:18:36.760
In order to survive these times of chaos,

00:18:36.920 --> 00:18:44.100
we concluded that we may want to form a friendship
with the Torqye Pashalu in the very near future.

00:18:44.220 --> 00:18:46.770
I would like you to take Abiriga with you

00:18:46.930 --> 00:18:50.060
to act as a bridge
between Venedik and Torqye.

00:18:50.480 --> 00:18:51.810
What are you talking about?

00:18:51.980 --> 00:18:54.400
Like we could ever trust you anymore.

00:18:54.570 --> 00:18:57.400
Abiriga is highly trusted
and accomplished.

00:18:57.570 --> 00:19:02.280
A talented man whose name is known
throughout Venedik.

00:19:02.450 --> 00:19:05.040
I promise that he will be of use to you.

00:19:05.200 --> 00:19:07.450
And if I refuse?

00:19:07.660 --> 00:19:09.960
With everything we've set in motion,

00:19:10.170 --> 00:19:12.670
we will not be able to keep Abiriga in the city,

00:19:12.830 --> 00:19:15.710
so we will likely send him to study abroad.

00:19:16.000 --> 00:19:17.170
I see.

00:19:17.340 --> 00:19:18.970
If that is the case,

00:19:19.170 --> 00:19:22.220
I will use this money to buy Abiriga from you.

00:19:23.260 --> 00:19:25.180
I've taken a liking to Abiriga.

00:19:25.350 --> 00:19:27.060
If you are sending him abroad anyway,

00:19:27.220 --> 00:19:29.270
would you sell him to me?

00:19:29.560 --> 00:19:30.980
Sold.

00:19:31.560 --> 00:19:33.310
In that case, from this day forward,

00:19:33.480 --> 00:19:39.280
I, Abiriga, will faithfully serve Mahmut Bey
as his humble attendant.

00:19:39.440 --> 00:19:40.900
Padrone.

00:19:46.410 --> 00:19:49.410
To think you would actually sell Abiriga...

00:19:49.750 --> 00:19:51.500
Doge Lucio,

00:19:51.670 --> 00:19:55.210
I had no choice but to respect his heart.

00:19:55.380 --> 00:19:57.840
What are your thoughts on the boy?

00:19:58.000 --> 00:19:59.970
I sense recklessness.

00:20:00.130 --> 00:20:02.550
However, he has lofty ideals
and is inexperienced.

00:20:02.720 --> 00:20:04.590
Qualities not well-suited for a soldier.

00:20:06.300 --> 00:20:09.810
The crafty realist
and the inexperienced idealist.

00:20:09.980 --> 00:20:12.310
Which do you think a nation needs?

00:20:12.640 --> 00:20:16.690
I would like to believe it's the former.

00:20:16.900 --> 00:20:18.820
The answer is both.

00:20:18.980 --> 00:20:21.450
The realist reins in the inexperienced,

00:20:21.610 --> 00:20:26.200
while inexperience makes up for the flaws
of realism with innovation.

00:20:26.530 --> 00:20:28.660
That inexperience is key.

00:20:28.830 --> 00:20:31.080
It is worth sending Abiriga to his side.

00:20:31.290 --> 00:20:33.210
I am surprised to hear you say that.

00:20:33.620 --> 00:20:37.000
I always thought of you
as the embodiment of a true realist.

00:20:37.170 --> 00:20:38.750
Even inside someone like me,

00:20:38.920 --> 00:20:41.380
there are seeds of idealism I cannot deny.

00:20:41.550 --> 00:20:44.220
I had thought you noticed.

00:20:44.340 --> 00:20:48.600
Is that not why you avoided telling me
of the Magistros' death?

00:20:48.760 --> 00:20:50.560
I apologize for taking liberties.

00:20:54.480 --> 00:20:56.190
Tughril Mahmut,

00:20:56.690 --> 00:20:59.230
let us stir up this chaotic world,

00:20:59.400 --> 00:21:01.690
and be swept away in return.

00:21:02.070 --> 00:21:03.110
Together.

00:21:04.240 --> 00:21:06.200
Are you sure about this, Mahmut Bey?

00:21:06.360 --> 00:21:12.290
That lanky bastard's definitely going to relay
everything we do back to Venedik.

00:21:12.540 --> 00:21:14.580
It is worth that risk.

00:21:14.750 --> 00:21:18.670
A time will undoubtedly come
when we'll need Venedik's help.

00:21:18.840 --> 00:21:20.920
Considering that,
this is a small price to pay.

00:21:21.960 --> 00:21:24.670
I apologize for deceiving you.

00:21:24.840 --> 00:21:26.260
Please forgive me.

00:21:26.430 --> 00:21:29.930
Venedik really loves
to beat around the bush, huh?

00:21:30.260 --> 00:21:33.060
I wonder what the Doge expected of me.

00:21:33.430 --> 00:21:35.140
I believe he took a liking to you.

00:21:35.310 --> 00:21:37.940
I don't think it's anything that complicated.

00:21:38.310 --> 00:21:41.480
You're talking about the same
all-logical and calculating guy we met?

00:21:43.030 --> 00:21:45.990
-Isn't that...?
-Yes, a bell from Phoinike.

00:21:46.530 --> 00:21:49.700
Doge Lucio had it built in the harbor.

00:21:49.990 --> 00:21:52.200
Logical and calculating...

00:21:52.410 --> 00:21:56.710
That doesn't mean he's lost his humanity.

00:21:57.000 --> 00:22:01.040
I knew that there were two sides to Venedik.

00:22:01.250 --> 00:22:04.550
Doge Lucio is the perfect representation
of a Venedikian.

00:22:04.880 --> 00:22:07.840
And you are Venedik itself as well.

00:23:48.820 --> 00:23:50.360
Birlik Torqye is being split apart?

00:23:50.820 --> 00:23:52.700
In a time when the threat of the Empire looms...

00:23:53.070 --> 00:23:55.410
Why, Sultan Balaban?

00:23:56.200 --> 00:23:58.450
Next time, "The Red Tiger Sultan."

00:23:58.620 --> 00:24:01.710
Darkness quashes the moonlight.
